{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.InterfaceScalar","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.triangle_phi3_has_four_terms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.triangle_phi3_has_four_terms","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L235-L240","doc":"**The chain really is different from the triangle.** With all three bonds present and equal\nthe cumulant stays negative, but the *reason* differs: there `φᵀ₃` has a sum of four terms, not\na single product. Exhibited so the chain collapse is not mistaken for a general fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.both_attractive_still_negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.both_attractive_still_negative","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L228-L233","doc":"**And uniform attraction is genuinely not enough** — a concrete both-above-`1` pair with a\nnegative cumulant, so `b3corpus_chain_neg_of_same_sign`'s first disjunct has content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.mixed_pair_gives_positive_b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.mixed_pair_gives_positive_b3","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L221-L226","doc":"**`(0,1)`-confinement is load-bearing, not decoration.** A mixed pair does give the AME\nsign, so `confined_bonds_force_b3_neg` is not vacuously true of everything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.confined_bonds_force_b3_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.confined_bonds_force_b3_neg","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L207-L217","doc":"**The one root, assembled.** If both chain bonds come from any family confined to `(0,1)` —\nthe production letters by `SingleCrossingAlwaysBinds.interface_mem_Ioo`, the isospin channels by\n`projector_bonds_lt_one` — then the connected three-body cumulant is negative. One hypothesis,\none conclusion; the three constructions differ only in what they compute *around* it.\n\nStated with the confinement as an explicit hypothesis rather than derived, so that a future\nfamily escaping `(0,1)` is visible as a failed hypothesis and not a hidden one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.attractive_projector_forces_negative_partner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.attractive_projector_forces_negative_partner","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L200-L205","doc":"**…and buying an attractive channel costs the partner its binding entirely.** If one\nisospin channel is made anti-binding (`μ₊ > 1`), the partition of unity puts the other at\n`μ₋ < 0`, where `−α·log μ₋` is not a real number. So the projector decomposition cannot host a\nsign-mixed bond pair even in principle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.projector_bonds_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.projector_bonds_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L193-L198","doc":"**The projector family cannot supply it either, and this is an identity not an\ninequality.** `μ₊ + μ₋ = 1` (`QBeta.InterfaceScalar.mu_sum_eq_one`), so two positive channel\nscalars are both below `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.production_chain_b3_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.production_chain_b3_neg","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L183-L191","doc":"**The production interface family is confined to `(0,1)`** — *not proved here*. That is\n`QBeta.SingleCrossingAlwaysBinds.interface_mem_Ioo` (`μ ≤ z < 1` whenever `q³ < q² + 1`, which\nthe substrate anchor satisfies with 24 % to spare). What this file adds is the consequence:\nfed into `b3corpus_chain_neg`, it makes the production chain negative whatever the typing. The\nhypothesis below is therefore stated as what it is — an input from that file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_pos_of_mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_pos_of_mixed","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L173-L179","doc":"**Restated as the mixed-sign requirement**, in the form the two `A = 3` chains impose:\none bond binding (`f < 1`) and the other anti-binding (`f > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L167-L171","doc":"**The sharp condition.** On a two-bond chain the cumulant is positive exactly when the two\nbonds lie on opposite sides of `1` — i.e. **exactly one** of them is attractive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_neg_of_same_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_neg_of_same_sign","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L151-L165","doc":"**🛑 THE CORRECTION — uniform attraction does not escape.** On a chain `φᵀ₃` is a product\nof two Mayer variables, so flipping *both* bonds from repulsive to attractive leaves the sign\nof `b₃` unchanged. Both cases in one statement: whenever the two bonds sit on the same side of\n`1`, `b₃ < 0`.\n\nSo \"a positive term needs a bond factor above 1\" is necessary, not sufficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain_neg","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L142-L149","doc":"**The chain is not covered by `b3corpus_neg`.** That theorem needs all three bond factors\nstrictly inside `(0,1)`; the chain's absent bond sits at exactly `1`. Supplied here: bonds in\n`(0,1)` on the two present edges still force `b₃ < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.b3corpus_chain","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L135-L138","doc":"The corpus three-body cumulant on a chain, in closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.phi3_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3SignOneRoot.phi3_chain","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3SignOneRoot.lean#L128-L133","doc":"**A missing bond is `f = 1`.** The production `A = 3` word bonds only adjacent nucleons,\nso one of the three pairs carries no interface letter; its Mayer variable is `g = f − 1 = 0`.\nOn that bond set the third Ursell function collapses from four connected graphs to one — the\nsingle path — and is a **product**. ","signatureChunk":0}]}